Compile the full (ONNX format) build without C++ exceptions.

Minimal builds never compile these files; a full build needs them:
- gsl::narrow exists only with exceptions; onnxruntime::narrow is ONNX Runtime's exception-free equivalent.
- Raw try/catch become ORT_TRY/ORT_CATCH, with handlers that read the exception inside ORT_HANDLE_EXCEPTION (the
  pattern ONNX Runtime uses elsewhere). Without exceptions the handlers are compiled out.
- JSON parsing in the model package code uses nlohmann::json's non-throwing parse (a discarded value on error) and
  strtoll instead of std::stoll.

